id=selinux_cosmetics
name=Shark8 GSI logspam cosmetics + MTK power fix
version=v5.3
versionCode=8
author=Bastet
description=Kills recurring GSI/vendor logspam on the Blackview Shark 8. (1) SELinux allow-rules for avc find/getattr/audit noise (pure allow, no permissive). (2) ImsProvisioningController tag at E. (3) patched /vendor/lib64/android.hardware.power-service-mediatek.so: mtkpower@impl [setMode] type:6 spam silenced, modes 2/3/5/7 unchanged. (4) patched /vendor/lib64/libpowerhal.so: [getCPUFreq] error cid:2, nClusterNum:2 ERROR silenced, plus the two absent perfNotifyAppState foreground-pid nodes (ta_fg_pid, gx_top_app_pid) repointed at /dev/null; all other libPowerHal errors kept. (5) libpowerhal.so: the whole netdagent error block silenced (8 log calls: dispatchNetdagentCmd failed/is not ok, SetPriorityWithUID fail, ClearPriorityWithUID fail, sdk_netd_*_by_linkinfo NetdAgentCmd/sprintf fail, no-more-empty-slot) - the vendor netdagent socket is commented out in /vendor/etc/init/netdagent.rc, so every net hint fails; the error returns themselves are kept. (6) persist.log.tag.libPowerHal/mtkpower_client/libPowerHal-bt=E: silences eara_io_service perf_lock_acq / [PE] update cmd noise and the BT low-latency INFO lines. (7) patched /vendor/lib64/lib_eara_io_scndet.so: eara_io@boost / eara_io@eval INFO firehose silenced (their '@' tags cannot be set as props), error paths kept. (8) patched /vendor/bin/netdagent: the daemon's own exec() res/status and run-command-failed ERROR lines silenced (iptables-wrapper exits 1 on this GSI).
